  "nextExperimentProposal": {
    "status": "proposal only; review required; no source modification or fit",
    "hypothesis": "Atomic public preference/product semantics are poorly preserved by a shared rank4 near-binary representation and singleton-only training; an additive seven-atom product head may transfer to unseen combinations.",
    "oneExperiment": "Separate product-only unsaturated 7-atom linear decoders from frozen centered native query/catalog vectors; auxiliary query multi-hot statedPreference and catalog multi-hot public-tag targets plus product cross-entropy, fixed equal loss weights, seed728/80epochs/AdamW.03/weightDecay.001. Average variant atom predictions per product, then dot with query atom prediction. Freeze existing centered image head/checkpoint unchanged.",
    "boundary": "Compute means from existing exact 28 TRAIN queries /42 TRAIN variants; derive atom targets only from those public TRAIN inputs; catalog auxiliary target counted once per unique variant. Distinct checkpoint/config and source freeze before held-out labels; never reuse old head as equivalent.",
    "architecture": "Two biased 4096->7 linear decoders: 57358 trainable product parameters. Product output uses raw linear atom predictions, no tanh bottleneck or hidden target/ID features. Existing image head frozen, outside new product parameter count.",
    "controls": "Independently trained item-only product prior, seeded random semantic head, query permutation; retain raw and guarded product/image counts, exact product-pair both-correct and flip metrics, atom decoding error per role. Explicit deterministic public-tag-overlap oracle is a teacher sanity check, not learned quality.",
    "feasibility": "Use already verified raw vectors only: zero native forwards, no cache writes. Request atom order is fixed seven-tag public vocabulary; decoder supervision is public factual distillation, not latent preference truth.",
